# Native YouTube Music provider

GPL-3.0. Catalog parsing and the original guest integration were adapted from MetroList at commit e97197786c2a7ad56279cc9bb4ce3233ef6c99ff. The standalone account, Home, JSON client configuration and plugin transport work are maintained by 956tris.

The build bundles InnerTubeX v0.11.7 from https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/innertubex/tree/v0.11.7 and QuackJS v0.1.4 from https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/quackjs/tree/v0.1.4. The host supplies Kotlin, coroutines, serialization, Ktor, Compose and MetroFuse API 1.1.0. Production code uses platform HTTP engine discovery, including on Android. The plugin owns its network client and session and does not read the application's old YouTube account.

This implementation provides search, catalog, metadata, Home, cookie account authentication and audio extraction. Authentication verifies an active account before committing credentials. The host stores credentials through its owner-scoped encrypted store. Failed account replacement preserves the previous session, and logout clears it. Login text is packaged in assets/login.json.

SABR sessions cross the public plugin API as the metrofuse.sabr.v1 JSON attribute on a SABR_UMP StreamDescriptor. The app validates the media identity, URL, format IDs and bounded session data, then creates its own InnerTubeX SabrBootstrap. Plugin-private classes are never passed into the app player.

Content locale comes from the system and Home request. Home titles come from the service. Library-linked Home shelves are excluded. Only the initial search/catalog browse page is exposed. Channel switching, library mutation, music videos and continuation loading remain outside this implementation.

See the repository README for builds, installation, verification and manual checks. JAR and APK files are published in GitHub Releases. The separate universal implementation in ../universal supports account, Home and direct audio without native payloads or full InnerTubeX player transforms.
